{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:96226",
  "title": "Important: nodejs:24 security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-10 00:04:46"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-10 00:14:42"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol (CVE-2026-19534)\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via uncontrolled recursion in nested brace patterns (CVE-2026-102278)\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via stack exhaustion from crafted brace patterns (CVE-2026-102276)\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via unhandled stream error on excessive content encodings (CVE-2026-109869)\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via TLS renegotiation with mismatched certificate (CVE-2026-87018)\n\n* undici: undici: Certificate validation bypass via dropped TLS options in Agent (CVE-2026-109383)\n\n* minimatch: minimatch: Denial of Service via crafted glob pattern expansion (CVE-2026-118764)\n\n* sqlite: sqlite: Denial of service via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5 (CVE-2026-119373)\n\n* sqlite: sqlite: Arbitrary code execution via crafted session changesets (CVE-2026-119379)\n\n* sqlite: sqlite: Arbitrary code execution via corrupted FTS5 index (CVE-2026-119374)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
